{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43743 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc255577 and Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of target interactions. Npc255577 is implicated in the target of multiple compounds, including WIL2-NS and (2E,4E)-1-(2-hydroxy-4-methoxy-5-methylphenyl)hexa-2,4-dien-1-one, which in turn target Phosphodiesterase 6C. Additionally, Npc255577 is also linked to JY, which targets SPQVJBJQVWOEOF-MKYGIPPKSA-N, which also targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings collectively indicate that Npc255577 may be a key player in the regulatory pathway leading to Phosphodiesterase 6C activation. The evidence suggests a possible functional link, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting Phosphodiesterase 6C through different intermediaries supports a broader role for Npc255577 in modulating this enzyme, potentially through indirect pathways.",
